From: Doruk Aktun <info@dorukaktun.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hi556: register the fwnode orientation and rotation

The driver never parses the device properties, so userspace cannot learn
where the sensor sits or how it is mounted, even when the firmware node
describes it. libcamera then warns "Failed to retrieve the camera
location" and assumes a rotation of 0 degrees. Parse the fwnode
properties and register V4L2_CID_CAMERA_ORIENTATION and
V4L2_CID_CAMERA_SENSOR_ROTATION, as most sensor drivers do.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
index 8cf4e3604..07d0bbec1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
@@ -847,12 +847,13 @@ static const struct v4l2_ctrl_ops hi556_ctrl_ops = {
 
 static int hi556_init_controls(struct hi556 *hi556)
 {
+	struct v4l2_fwnode_device_properties props;
 	struct v4l2_ctrl_handler *ctrl_hdlr;
 	s64 exposure_max, h_blank;
 	int ret;
 
 	ctrl_hdlr = &hi556->ctrl_handler;
-	ret = v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(ctrl_hdlr, 8);
+	ret = v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(ctrl_hdlr, 10);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -903,6 +904,13 @@ static int hi556_init_controls(struct hi556 *hi556)
 				     V4L2_CID_TEST_PATTERN,
 				     ARRAY_SIZE(hi556_test_pattern_menu) - 1,
 				     0, 0, hi556_test_pattern_menu);
+
+	ret = v4l2_fwnode_device_parse(hi556->dev, &props);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	v4l2_ctrl_new_fwnode_properties(ctrl_hdlr, &hi556_ctrl_ops, &props);
+
 	if (ctrl_hdlr->error)
 		return ctrl_hdlr->error;
 
